# AI-103 Lesson 18 -- copy to .env and fill in. Gitignored.
#
# Everything here is KEYLESS. Every Content Understanding sample on Microsoft
# Learn uses an `Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key` header, and this lesson deliberately
# does not. A key would work, and it would also hide the exact permission
# problem this lesson wants you to be able to diagnose.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Foundry account that hosts Content Understanding
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Content Understanding is a data plane ON a Foundry (AIServices) account. There
# is no separate "Content Understanding resource" to create, which surprises
# people who went looking for one in the portal.
#
# This MUST be the custom-subdomain host:
#     https://<account-name>.cognitiveservices.azure.com
# NOT a regional host (https://eastus2.api.cognitive.microsoft.com). Entra ID
# token auth binds to the subdomain; a regional host has no subdomain to bind
# to and will hand you a 401 that looks like a bad token.
#
# Find it: Foundry portal -> your account -> Overview -> Endpoint. Or:
#   az cognitiveservices account show -n <account> -g <rg> --query properties.endpoint -o tsv
#
# Trailing slashes are stripped by load_settings(), so either form is fine.
CONTENT_UNDERSTANDING_ENDPOINT=https://<foundry-account>.cognitiveservices.azure.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API version
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2025-11-01 is the GA version. Say that out loud when you teach this: a very
# large amount of Content Understanding material still in circulation targets
# 2024-12-01-preview or 2025-05-01-preview, and those are not merely older, they
# are wrong in breaking ways. Notably the preview `scenario` property is gone,
# and preview allowed inheriting from analyzers that GA rejects.
#
# Verify what your account actually serves before you record:
#   $t = az account get-access-token --resource https://cognitiveservices.azure.com --query accessToken -o tsv
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" -H "Authorization: Bearer $t" `
#     "https://<account>.cognitiveservices.azure.com/contentunderstanding/analyzers?api-version=2025-11-01"
# A 404 here means the api-version is not served, NOT that the path is wrong.
CONTENT_UNDERSTANDING_API_VERSION=2025-11-01

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Models -- Content Understanding is bring-your-own
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any analyzer carrying a fieldSchema needs a completion model. Managed capacity
# for generative analyzers was retired at GA, so the service will not quietly
# supply one. These are model NAMES, resolved against the deployment defaults
# registered on the resource -- they are not deployment names, and that
# indirection is why this file stays portable across lesson environments.
#
# Inspect what your resource has registered:
#   curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $t" `
#     "https://<account>.cognitiveservices.azure.com/contentunderstanding/defaults?api-version=2025-11-01"
#
# If that returns an empty modelDeployments object, register them with
# PATCH /contentunderstanding/defaults before any custom analyzer will build.
# The build failure names this exact fix, which is unusually kind of it:
#   "This analyzer needs a 'completion' model deployment for current request,
#    but none was resolved."
CU_COMPLETION_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
CU_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-large

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RBAC you need on the account (data plane, assigned to the human running this)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Three Content Understanding roles shipped in May 2026:
#   Cognitive Services Content Understanding Reader       read, list, analyze
#   Cognitive Services Content Understanding Contributor  + create, update
#   Cognitive Services Content Understanding Owner        + DELETE
#
# Beat 3 deletes the analyzer it creates, so you want OWNER. Contributor builds
# and runs an analyzer perfectly well and then fails the cleanup with a 403,
# which is a genuinely surprising place to find a permissions wall.
#
# Cognitive Services User (the L04 convention) also works for the read paths.
# Owner on the subscription grants NONE of this: that is control plane, and
# every call in this lesson is data plane.
